    11	 * `next_run_at`): a streaming feed is written with `virtual = false`, `kind =
    12	 * 'streaming'`, AND its sync-lifecycle columns (`schedule` / `next_run_at` /
    13	 * `checkpoint`) left NULL, so `check-due-feeds` never queues it (it also filters
    14	 * `kind = 'collected'` explicitly). Both guards hold here.
    15	 *
    16	 * Multi-replica safe + idempotent WITHOUT a unique constraint on
    17	 * (connection_id, feed_key): the fast path is a lock-free SELECT (the common
    18	 * case after the first bind); the slow path takes a transaction-scoped advisory
    19	 * lock on the (connection, feed_key) tuple, re-checks, then inserts — so two
    20	 * replicas binding the same channel concurrently can't create duplicates.
